    "Values represent per-instruction energy cost in picojoules at ~3.0 GHz, 1.0V (typical Skylake).",
    "x86-64 instructions cost 1.5-3x more than equivalent ARM A55 instructions due to complex decode and out-of-order execution.",
    "Load/store costs reflect L1 cache hits; cache misses incur 5-25x additional energy.",
    "SIMD/AVX costs are per-execution; actual cost depends on vector width and µop decomposition.",
    "LLVM internal opcode names (e.g. ADD32rr) are included alongside canonical ASM mnemonics.",
    "Unknown opcodes return 0.0 pJ — treat as accounted for elsewhere or contribute negligibly.",
    "Values are derived from published measurements and scaled relative to ARM Cortex-A55 baseline, consistent with the ~2x per-instruction energy gap between x86 and ARM at comparable process nodes."
